Original commit body from 1fe61c0cb3a685fbb7d92bc6883f3a2ec3bc91ed:

§14's origin condition tested PASS-ID INEQUALITY and stood in for a test on
INDEPENDENT OBSERVATION. A single-backend Python run of this repository
demoted 419 stubs, every superseder a LINKER — and those 419 superseders were
419 of the 421 edges inherited-calls-linker (329 of 329) and
method-call-recovery-linker (90 of 92) emitted. Each superseding edge is that
linker's own resolution of the very stub it superseded, built from the stub's
src, line and parsed callee, so the four-part key matched BY CONSTRUCTION.
The pass was rediscovering a derivation, not detecting a contradiction. §13
case 2 in contrapositive: a refinement of one observation is not a second one.

45 of the 419 are false, every one from method-call-recovery-linker, whose
receiver-type filter drops a hint that CONTRADICTS a declared
receiver_type_hint but abstains when none is stamped — and none of the 90
carried one. 28 of the 45 demoted a stub whose external key was COMPLETE and
CORRECT (tree_sitter_rust.language, builtins.id) in favour of a
same-short-name in-repo FIELD. inherited-calls-linker was right on 70 of 70
audited and consistent with the declared inheritance graph on 329 of 329.

Two conditions added, for six:

- the stub must have ABSTAINED on its module. ir.stated_module_of is promoted
  from merge_producers as the one reader of that fact, so §14 and §15's fold
  cannot drift (INV-difud is what two homes for one read costs). A complete
  key contradicts an in-repo answer rather than being filled by it, and §11
  makes a dst disagreement two edges.
- both sides must be an ANCHORED PRODUCER's edge, via the new
  registry.anchored_producer_tokens. It accepts the analyzer name and the
  backend name, because the SCIP arms stamp origin="scip" while registering
  as rust_analyzer / scip_python; that divergence is filed as INV-gabak.

The language gate stays a registry query — what it reads there is a
DECLARATION (the incumbent's name_key), not an observation; analysis_runs
carries no pass-kind field and Edge.origin answers per edge (§15.3). Under
the new conditions the gate is provably redundant, so a single-backend run is
byte-identical through §14, as it already was through §3.

Measured: 419 -> 0, no node or edge added or removed, no confidence or
is_resolved changed, and the only rank_score changes across 207,486 shared
edges are those 419. Both two-backend recorded fixtures untouched
(aardvark-dns 3, scip-python sample 1).

The old control could not have caught this: it popped the producer from the
REGISTRY, which short-circuits the pass before the origin gate. Renamed to
test_a_language_with_one_registered_producer_is_untouched (it does test that
gate) and joined by one that leaves the registry as production has it and
varies the graph instead.

Cost, stated: 374 true-or-probably-true supersessions (115 hand-verified, 259
screened-but-unread) go unrecorded until the consuming pass stamps the stub
it derived from — filed as WI-togad, blocked by WI-latup. The residual false
binds themselves are filed as WI-rulik.

Also fixes a pre-existing red on dev: cmd_backend_agreement wrote --out with
a bare Path.write_text, bypassing safety_zones.user_out_write and INV-zudak's
live guard.

Files WI-rulik, INV-gabak, WI-togad.

